Z||000018||Oreif||04-19-2000||01:22 AM||||Cobra, Think what you want. What is it with you anyways? If it's not done your way you whine? If you can't understand the concept you nitpick it?<P><BR>        6_4_2<BR>        5_3_1<P>____5<BR>__4___6<BR>__3___1<BR>____2<P>If it's the letters that confuse you, I have put the numbers of the cylinders with their respective positions on the distributor. If you still can't grasp the concept, there's nothing else to say. <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 04-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||Cliff Pennock||04-19-2000||03:37 AM||||Cobra, you are absolutely right. My drawing does in no way tell you what the firing order is. It's just a drawing I made when someone asked me how the wires should go. I simply walked up to my car and jotted down what was connected to what. When I made it, I realised that I didn't know the firing order so I used letters instead of numbers. I gave the top left cylinder the letter 'A', the bottom left cylinder 'B', etc. It really is nothing more than a coincidence that had I reversed the order of the letters it would also give you the firing order!<P>I'll revise the drawing so next time there won't be any confusion.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
